RESOLUTION NO. 2026-049
A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CHINO,
CALIFORNIA, ORDERING THE SUBMISSION TO THE QUALIFIED ELECTORS
OF THE CITY OF A GENERAL TAX MEASURE ADDING CHAPTER 5.03 TO
THE CHINO MUNICIPAL CODE MODERNIZING THE CITY’S BUSINESS
LICENSE TAX AT THE GENERAL MUNICIPAL ELECTION TO BE HELD ON
TUESDAY, NOVEMBER 3, 2026; SETTING RULES FOR FILING WRITTEN
ARGUMENTS, IMPARTIAL ANALYSIS, REBUTTALS, AND PUBLIC
EXAMINATION; AND DIRECTING RELATED ACTIONS
WHEREAS, a General Election on Tuesday, November 3, 2026 has been called by
Resolution No. 2026-035, adopted by the City Council on June 2, 2026; and
WHEREAS, the City of Chino (“City”) currently imposes a business license tax on persons
conducting business in the City pursuant to Chapter 5.04 of the Chino Municipal Code; and
WHEREAS, the City Council desires to submit to the qualified voters of the City a measure
that, if approved, would repeal conflicting provisions of the City’s existing business license tax
structure in Chapter 5.04 of the Chino Municipal Code and add Chapter 5.03 to the Municipal Code
to establish a more modern and equitable business license tax based on gross receipts attributable
to business activity conducted in the City, with maximum rates based on business type and a reduced
$25 tax for the first $75,000 or less in gross receipts; and
WHEREAS, the proposed measure is a general tax measure because the revenues would
be deposited in the City’s General Fund and available for unrestricted general governmental
purposes, including but not limited to, police and 911 response, streets, public area safety and
cleanliness, protecting local drinking water sources, and other general City services; and
WHEREAS, Article XIII C, section 2(b) of the California Constitution provides that no local
government may impose, extend, or increase a general tax unless and until that tax is submitted to
the electorate and approved by a majority vote, and further requires that the election be consolidated
with a regularly scheduled general election for members of the governing body, except in cases of
emergency declared by unanimous vote; and
WHEREAS, Government Code sections 53723 and 53724, Elections Code section 9222,
and other applicable law authorize the City Council to submit the proposed general tax measure and
ordinance to the voters of the City; and
WHEREAS, pursuant to Government Code section 53724, the measure must be proposed
by ordinance or resolution of the legislative body and the ordinance or resolution must include the
type and rate of tax to be levied, the method of collection, and the date upon which the election shall
be held; and
