SECTION 6. Nature of Tax; Majority Approval Required.
The measure is a general tax measure. The proceeds of the business license tax imposed
by the Ordinance shall be deposited into the City’s General Fund and may be used for any lawful
general governmental purpose. The measure shall be approved if it receives a majority of the votes
cast on the measure.
SECTION 7. Tax Type, Rates, Method of Collection, and Duration.
The tax proposed by the Ordinance is a business license tax imposed on persons conducting
business in the City. The tax is measured by gross receipts attributable to business activity
conducted in the City, with maximum rates ranging from $0.60 to $1.50 per $1,000 of gross receipts
based on business type, and with a $25 tax for businesses with $75,000 or less in gross receipts.
The tax shall be administered and collected by the City Tax Collector or the Tax Collector’s designee
as provided in the Ordinance and shall continue until ended by voters.
