5.03.130 Delinquent Taxes (Penalties and Interest)
(a) The business license tax in this chapter shall be due and payable and a penalty of ten percent
shall be added to each license remaining unpaid thirty days after it becomes due. On the first
day of each month thereafter that such tax remains unpaid, an additional penalty of ten percent
of such unpaid tax shall be added; provided, that the maximum penalty amount shall not
exceed an amount equal to 100% of the amount of the original license tax.
